- which pattern forms are core to Ferox;
- which tempting pattern extensions should stay out of scope;
- what makes the chosen pattern surface easier to reason about and implement;
- how formatter, parser, and diagnostics should reinforce that discipline.

Include canonical examples, out-of-scope examples, a validation/test plan, and logging expectations for parser, lowering, and diagnostic behavior around patterns.

